  "//speed": "World voxels per second at a cruise: 3.5 m/s. It circles at the behaviour's orbit.speed (1.3x, ~4.5 m/s, a lap in ~3 s) and charges at chargeSpeed (5x) under the body's own burst ceiling (swim.burst 5x): about 17.5 m/s -- a mako's burst. accel 300 takes it from the circle to the top of the run inside half a second; brake 160 is the glide that carries it ~80 voxels past you before it swings back onto the next lap.",
  "speed": 35,
  "locomotion": {
    "turnRate": 3.6,
    "turnAccel": 16,
    "turnRateMoving": 1.0,
    "driveAlignFull": 0.6,
    "driveAlignZero": 2.4
  },
  "//swim": "MobDef::SwimDef. A slow pitch (it does not stand on its tail), a soft accel and a softer brake (it glides), fins that hold it on its line, neutral buoyancy. surfaceGap 0.5: the back cruises half a voxel under, so the dorsal fin cuts the surface when it rides high; a charge may lift the back 1.5 over (breach) to take a man treading water. Out of the water: 10 s of breath, then 25 hp a second; it flops toward water it can feel within 10 voxels.",
  "swim": {
    "pitchRate": 1.8,
    "maxPitch": 0.9,
    "accel": 300,
    "brake": 160,
    "sideGrip": 7,
    "burst": 5,
    "buoyancy": 1,
    "surfaceGap": 0.2,
    "bedGap": 1,
    "breach": 1.5,
    "feel": 7,
    "bank": 0.7,
    "maxRoll": 0.8,
    "//fins": "A BODY MISSING A FIN (MobDef::SwimDef::FinDef, DESIGN.md \"Swimmers\"). The pectorals start its pitch changes, pivot its turns and flare to brake; the tail is its thrust (Wilga & Lauder 2000). Each fin's share is its voxels left over its voxels at spawn. One pectoral gone: turns toward the stump at half rate (turnLoss) so it circles toward its good side; a hard brake -- the end of a charge -- spins it toward the fin it has (brakeSpin 2.5 rad/s at full brake, steering loosened while it lasts), so a missed pass ends in a skid, flank first; it lists toward the stump (listRoll ~17 deg, more when slow) and rolls with every climb and dive. Both gone: no trim -- it sinks (sink, a quarter of gravity when slow, less at speed), wallows, and its burst falls to a lunge. The tail gone: three quarters of the thrust (thrustLoss). Losing 15% of a fin at once or bite by bite (thrashMin) throws it into up to 2.5 s of flailing (thrash) that bites nothing.",
    "fins": { "left": "fin.L", "right": "fin.R", "tail": "tail", "turnLoss": 0.5, "brakeSpin": 2.5, "brakeLoss": 0.5, "listRoll": 0.3, "pitchRoll": 0.15, "sink": 0.25, "thrustLoss": 0.75, "thrash": 2.5, "thrashMin": 0.15 },
    "breathSeconds": 10,
    "suffocateHp": 25,
    "flopMin": 0.5,
    "flopMax": 1.4,
    "flopRise": 1.2,
    "flopSpeed": 1,
    "flopReach": 10,
    "//wave": "CARANGIFORM: a stiff front (ampHead 0.08) and the swing growing all the way to the tail (ampRamp 1), a body-length wave on a clock -- 0.55 beats a second hanging still, plus the speed over slip x wavelength cruising -- so the tail beats faster than the body goes. The turn lays the body on its arc (turnBend), capped low: a shark is stiff.",
